		answer: `Government surveys indicate that 87% of Malawians are Christian and 11.6% are Muslim. Catholics are 36.3% of the population and the Church of Central Africa Presbyterian (CCAP) 18%, with 1.3 million members. You can read the Scriptures they treasure free in Father's Heart Bible™ at fathersheartbible.com/read.`,
	},
